    "body": "Something I was thinking of (definitely not a long-term solution, just something for this issue). I technically don't need a `simulator_quimb` since I can just define the quimb circuit in `.to_matrix` and get the unitary there.\n```py\ndef to_matrix(self):\n        import quimb.gates\n        import quimb.tensor as qtn\n        from tequila import compile_circuit\n\n        compiled_circuit = compile_circuit(self)\n\n        gate_mapping = {\n            'Rx': quimb.gates.RX,\n            'Ry': quimb.gates.RY,\n            'Rz': quimb.gates.RZ\n        }\n\n        quimb_circuit = qtn.Circuit(self.n_qubits)\n\n        for g in compiled_circuit.gates:\n            if g.is_parameterized():\n                quimb_circuit.apply_gate(\n                    gate_mapping[g.name],\n                    g.parameter,\n                    g.target\n                )\n            elif g.is_controlled():\n                quimb_circuit.apply_gate(\n                    quimb.gates.CX,\n                    g.control,\n                    g.target\n                )\n\n        uni = quimb_circuit.get_uni()\n        unitary = np.array(uni.to_dense())\n        return unitary\n```\nI say this for one main reason:\n- I can't just add `simulator_quimb` and add/update its simulate to return unitary instead of `QubitWaveFunction` because it will introduce inconsistency in the simulator API. So, I'd have to make a new method for it to return the unitary.\n- Major issue with this is that I can't just add that to `simulator_quimb`. I would have to add it to base, and then add NotImplementedError to other backends, and then add it to quimb's simulator.\n\nIf you want I can do that, or I can propose the small one above for now. What do you think? This one is definitely easier to merge since it doesn't break the api, just adds a new method to `QCircuit`, and makes quimb a local import like requested. The other is a much larger task (worthwhile IFF I add unitary to all the backends which is not a problem as long as they support it) and would be nice as a backend api extension feature.",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "pin": null,
