    "updated_at": "2025-05-28T14:34:30Z",
    "body": "Cool!\n\nThe second option would be great, because it adds quimb as a full simulation backend (worth more than the to_matrix functionality; but I didn't thought about it when setting up the issue). With to_matrix as a method in the backends: Would be sufficient to have `raise NotImplementedError` in the base and then only implement it in the quimb interface for now (no need to have this available for all backends). \n\nThe proposed solution however works for the issue here. \nOne thing that needs to be taken care of, is that quimb will (most likely) not be able to give me back a parametrized unitary (or is it?). Solution for this is to force `to_matrix` to set the parameters of the circuit: \n\n```python\ndef to_matrix(circuit, variables)\n    ...\n    compiled_circuit = compiled_circuit.map_variables(variables)\n    ...\n```\n",
