    "body": "Take for example\n```python\nU = tq.gates.Ry(angle=\"a\", target=0)\n```\n\nThis initializes an $R_y$ with an angle $a$ whose value is not yet specified. \nTechnically the matrix of this circuit is\n$e^{-i a/2 Y} = \\cos(a/2) -i \\sin(a/2)Y$\n\nwhich is\n```python\n[\n[cos(a/2), -sin(a/2),\n[sin(a/2), cos(a/2)]\n]\n```\n\nbut this is a matrix of abstract functions.\n\nAfter you do for example\n```python\nU = U.map_variables({\"a\":1.0} \n```\nThe variable \"a\" has been set to a real number.\n",
    "author_association": "COLLABORATOR",
